Alembic migrations for PumpAtlas AI.

The initial schema is applied from db/schema.sql (generated from the models by
scripts/gen_schema.py), together with db/extensions.sql, db/functions.sql and
db/rls.sql. Alembic then owns every change after that point.

    # after changing a model
    python scripts/gen_schema.py                     # refresh db/schema.sql
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add field X" # generate the migration
    alembic upgrade head                             # apply it

Autogenerate does not manage RLS policies, triggers or the text search configuration.
Those live in db/*.sql; if a change touches them, add the statement to the migration by
hand with op.execute().
